{
 "version": "13.3.0",
 "date": "2026-11-23",
 "notes": [
  "Three books added to the Roman Catholic and Eastern Orthodox topics (owner request, from a video recommending them): Martin Chemnitz, Examination of the Council of Trent; Joshua Schooping, Disillusioned; Matthew Barrett, The Reformation as Renewal.",
  "Six new answer cards (217 in all):",
  "Roman Catholicism: \"Scripture and Tradition together are the word of God\" (Chemnitz's eight kinds of tradition, seven accepted and one refused); \"Protestantism began in 1517. Where was your church before Luther?\" (Calvin's reply to Sadoleto, the Reformation confessions, Barrett's argument); \"The Church has always believed in purgatory\" (Chemnitz's history; Augustine still unsure around 420).",
  "Eastern Orthodoxy: \"The church has always venerated icons\" (the Council of Elvira, Epiphanius, Gregory the Great, the councils of 787 and 794); \"Christians have always prayed to the saints\" (two hundred years of silence; Origen's hesitation); \"Orthodoxy is the unchanged Church of the apostles\" (Schooping's case from the inside).",
  "The books are now on the reading lists of six existing cards: tradition, icons, prayer to the saints, justification, the Mass and the \"unchanging Church.\" No existing argument was reworded.",
  "What was actually read. Chemnitz: the relevant sections of the whole work in the original Latin, which is in the public domain; his words on the cards are translated from it. Barrett: the publisher's free sample (contents and first chapter). Schooping: the book was not available, so the cards rely on the publisher's description, three published reviews (including a chapter-by-chapter review in the Puritan Reformed Journal) and readers' chapter summaries, and say so. Every Bible quotation is the Berean Standard Bible, checked by tools/checkquotes.py; the other quotations are from public-domain documents checked at their sources."
 ],
